00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:33.960
Uh, in the beginning, the Divine Speech program is broken up into two parts.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:35.660
So today and tomorrow.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.550
Today's agenda

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:43.250
is basically what I like to call micro studies. Micro studies.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.650
and tomorrow's agenda is macro studies. Now that's technical terms.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:49.250
So let's make that easier to understand.

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:54.540
Micro means we're going to try to understand some things about the aayah of the Quran

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:57.250
or how Allah uses certain kinds of words.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:01.170
Or how Allah uses things at the very small, you know,

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:05.349
zoomed in, or kind of, take a microscope and put it to the Quran

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:08.450
and look at a very zoomed in view of how the Quran is structured.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.880
Tomorrow we're going to look at the Quran in a different way.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.460
We're gonna kind of take a look, take a step back

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.260
and look at the bigger picture.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.960
We're going to look at how the surah is organized.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.760
How the stories are spread all over the Quran.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.750
Why does Allah take oaths in the Quran.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.360
How come Allah repeats Himself so much in the Quran? Bigger picture questions.

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.120
So those are two different kinds of views.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.650
You know, I like to compare it to when you're in a garden.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:39.050
If you're sitting in a garden somewhere and you're staring at a flower,

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.460
then you're zooming in.

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:43.590
You take your camera and you zoom in and you're

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:46.390
kind of taking this close up shot of the camera.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:50.960
But when you do that, you lose sight of the fact that you're in the middle of a valley

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.080
and there are other trees and rivers and everything else

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.860
because you're so focused on the beauty of one flower.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:00.310
But when you're flying over in a helicopter or an airplane

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:02.780
or you're standing on top of the mountain looking down,

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.070
you see a different kind of beauty.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:07.350
The beauty is of the entire scene, you understand?

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.560
So there's two different kinds of beauty.

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:10.380
Beauty

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.530
when you pay attention at the micro level,

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.690
when you zoom in. And beauty when you take a

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:17.150
step back and you look at the bigger picture.

