You go to Chapter Two, you go to Chapter Three.

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:25.070
You go to Chapter Four. When you go to Chapter Four

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:27.760
they will never repeat what they taught you in Chapter what?

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:28.860
One.

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:30.250
They will not.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:33.470
They will take the concepts that they are already covered in

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:36.900
One, Two, and Three and then build that in number Four.

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:37.560
Yes?

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:42.260
And if they have to remind you of something from Chapter One, what do they do?

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:44.460
Refer back to

00:12:45.340 --> 00:12:46.150
Chapter One.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:50.200
They'll put a footnote in the book and say, go back to page this.

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:52.880
Go back to page that, this has already been talked about.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:56.150
We already previously discussed this. See page 81.

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:58.030
You see, you see that in books?

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:01.120
The idea of chapters is that they build

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:03.860
an argument little by little by little chronologically.

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:08.760
And the other thing about chapters is if you change the sequence of the chapters.

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:12.250
If you take Chapter Ten and you make it Chapter Three

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:16.560
And you take Chapter Two and make it Chapter Five, does the book makes sense anymore?

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:17.850
No.

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:21.240
Is it possible somebody has only studied

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:22.360
Surat al-Kawthar

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:26.520
and somebody else has studied Surat al-Baqarah, and it may still make sense?

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.150
Is that possible in the Quran?

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:30.260
So it's not like a chapter.

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:33.650
From a literature perspective, it's not like a chapter.

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:36.060
The other thing about chapters is,

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:39.460
especially for something historical, the Quran is historical,

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:41.960
the chapters have a certain

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:43.450
chronology.

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:46.640
The earliest writing is at the beginning,

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:49.420
then the later writing, then the later writing, then the later writing.

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:53.250
In other words, there should be some kind of order in chapters. Subject order.

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:57.290
Chronological order. Is the Quran in chronological order? Is it

00:13:57.290 --> 00:13:59.220
that the earliest surah is in the beginning,

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:01.270
then the later one, then the later one, then the later one.

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:01.960
Is it like that?

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:06.110
If the Quran was in chronological order, then it would be

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:09.590
ٱقۡرَأۡ بِٱسۡمِ رَبِّكَ ٱلَّذِی خَلَقَ
in the beginning.

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:10.150
Right?

00:14:10.630 --> 00:14:14.390
And aayaat of Surat al-Baqarah, some of the aayaat, would be at the very end.

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:18.940
It would be a completely different order. So the Quran is not in chronological order.

00:14:19.030 --> 00:14:21.450
The Quran is not in chapter order.

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:25.230
The Quran is not organized by size.

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:28.960
If it was by size al-Baqarah would be surah number one.

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:31.550
Al-Kawthar would be surah number 114.

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:33.200
It's not by size.

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:37.350
Oh, I know. Maybe the Quran is organized by subject.

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:40.060
It's organized by subject.

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:41.860
Is it organized by subject?

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:43.250
No.

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:44.360
I mean,

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:46.110
if you say, what is the subject of Surat

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:48.060
al-Baqarah, it is very difficult to answer that question.

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:50.560
It's very difficult.

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:51.660
Because

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:55.150
everything in the Quran is in Surat al-Baqarah.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:15:00.280
ُلِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ سَنامٌ وسَنامُ الْقُرْآنِ اَلبَقَرَة

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:01.490
Everything has a peak.

00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:03.740
The peak of the Quran is al-Baqarah. All the themes of

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:06.590
the Quran are inside al-Baqarah. So you can't even point at Surat al-Baqarah

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:10.050
and say, this is the subject of Surah al-Baqarah. You can't do it.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:13.180
As a matter of fact, when you go to a surah like Surat

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:17.870
Ibrahim, you can't say, oh, I know what Surat Ibrahim is about. It's about Ibrahim!

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:21.470
'Alayhissalaaam. Uh, no, actually, when you start reading Surat Ibrahim,

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:24.160
you're gonna find a lot of things that have nothing to do with

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:28.250
Ibrahim 'alayhissalaam. Oh, Surat al-Baqarah it must be 286

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:29.430
aayaat about cows.

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:32.650
Does that happen?

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:35.060
No.

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:37.160
A cow comes up,

00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:40.560
but there's a lot of things that have nothing to do with beef.

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:44.080
You understand?

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:45.960
You know, chapters have a title.

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:48.950
Usually chapters have a heading, a name.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:52.960
And that name tells you everything about the chapter.

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:54.550
Does the Quran do that?

00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:55.760
No.

00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:59.730
So it is in my view, اَلله أَعْلَم, it is

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:04.160
incorrect from a literature perspective, to call the surah a

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:05.360
chapter.

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:10.210
It's unique. It's its own entity. There is no other book that has surahs.

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:11.050
That's only Quran.

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:13.080
Every other book can have chapters,

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:14.160
sections.

00:16:14.730 --> 00:16:15.680
Quran has surahs.

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:20.070
In other words Allah from the very beginning set His own standard.

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:22.460
You see, when you write an essay

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:26.110
and you hand it to your teacher, your teacher corrects it and says,

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:27.990
you should break the paragraph over here.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.930
You should put the capital letter over here.

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:33.630
You should reorganize the subject over here. Take this sentence out. Why?

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:38.260
Because there is a standard and you are not meeting the standard. Isn't that true?

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:41.900
But the Quran came with its own standard.

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:44.680
So you don't, you cannot actually,

00:16:44.680 --> 00:16:47.240
from the very beginning, I want you to understand this idea,

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:50.360
you cannot compare the Quran to any

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:53.130
other literature because from the very beginning,

00:16:53.140 --> 00:16:56.850
the units of any book are chapters and the units of the Quran are

00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:58.040
surahs.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:58.850
You can't do it.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:04.319
This is the biggest mistake of, you know, non-Muslim scholarship about the Quran.

00:17:04.329 --> 00:17:06.670
They compare it to other literature and say, well,

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:09.170
the Quran, its chapters don't make any sense.

00:17:09.609 --> 00:17:11.980
It's chapters are unorganized. And I say,

00:17:12.089 --> 00:17:13.460
Listen, my kaafir friend,

00:17:14.839 --> 00:17:16.200
these aren't chapters,

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:18.560
so you're missing the point altogether.

00:17:19.839 --> 00:17:23.079
Now, inside the chapter, the surahs are made up of what?

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:25.460
What is inside the chapter?

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:27.550
Oh sorry, inside the surah? What's inside?

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:29.050
Aayah.

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:30.550
Aayah.

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:34.160
Now sometimes we translate aayah as what?

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:36.450
We translate it as 'verse'.

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:38.960
I have a real problem with that too.

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:41.780
In the English language,

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:45.520
especially in the American context and possibly even the European,

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:46.790
the British, the Australian, and

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:50.350
other contexts, the word verse is used in two ways.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:54.170
We need to understand these things because they have implications.

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:56.520
The word verse is used in two ways.

00:17:56.740 --> 00:18:01.160
The first way the word verse is used is when you're talking about poetry,

00:18:02.240 --> 00:18:04.960
verses of a song or verses of a poem.

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:09.970
You've heard this before, right? Verses of a song or verses of

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:11.160
a poem.

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:17.080
This is problematic to call, the aayaat of the Quran to be called verses. It

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:19.860
is as though we are comparing the aayaat of the Quran to what?

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:21.860
Poetry.

00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:26.260
the problem with that is the Quran emphatically says

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:29.140
وَمَا عَلَّمۡنَـٰهُ ٱلشِّعۡرَ

00:18:29.220 --> 00:18:30.380
We didn't teach him poetry.

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:31.780
وَمَا هُوَ بِقَوۡلِ شَاعِرࣲۚ

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:34.110
It is not the word of a poet.

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:36.650
وَٱلشُّعَرَاۤءُ یَتَّبِعُهُمُ ٱلۡغَاوُۥنَ

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:38.460
Poets, they don't know what they're talking about.

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:42.640
and people who have completely, are completely lost, they follow them.

00:18:42.670 --> 00:18:47.450
In other words, the Quran is very strong in declaring that it has nothing to do with

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:48.760
poetry.

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:49.950
So when we use the word verse,

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:51.920
there's already a problem in the English

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:55.750
speaking mind because there's an association with

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:56.860
poetry,

00:18:57.540 --> 00:18:58.520
which is a problem.

00:18:59.140 --> 00:19:01.390
Here's the second kind of,  so the first thing was it

00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:03.030
has to do something with poetry or songs.

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:04.170
The second issue

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:07.800
is that verses usually come up when we talk about verses of the Bible.

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:11.600
In the English speaking world, the European world

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:13.000
and part of the European world,

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:16.260
and, of course, the colonized European world, the Americas,

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:18.060
the Australias of the world, etcetera,

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:20.760
when we think of verse, we think of verse of the

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:21.670
Bible,

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:23.660
which is also problematic

00:19:24.740 --> 00:19:26.740
because when you want people to think about the Quran,

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:28.060
we don't want them to think about what?

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:29.660
The Bible.

00:19:30.740 --> 00:19:31.740
As a matter of fact,

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:35.000
there are allegations made by Western scholars that

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:37.760
the Quran stole its information from the Bible.

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:43.990
They say that the Quran, it's information, ma'aadh Allah, the Prophet ﷺ

00:19:44.060 --> 00:19:47.280
used to travel, used to trade. And he traded in Syria,

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:50.190
and he traded in, you know, in different parts, some Christian parts.

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:53.360
And he heard some of those stories and he mixed them up and he put them in the Quran.

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:57.670
So it's actually taken from the People of the Book.

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:01.350
We don't want even to give the hint

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:03.770
that it has anything to do

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:05.770
with the Bible, actually.

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:09.140
because what is left of the Bible is actually

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:11.600
something that has been tampered with by human beings.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.770
I don't want to give that association at all.

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:18.770
And so I would have to say that the definition of an aayah

00:20:19.140 --> 00:20:21.560
is also like the definition of surah,

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:22.760
unique.

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:28.170
Somebody said to me, maybe aayah could be translated as 'sentence'.

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:30.370
The sentences of the Quran.

00:20:30.590 --> 00:20:32.460
Let me tell you why that's impossible.

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:35.460
The first aayah of Surah al-Baqarah is what?

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:39.160
Alif. Laam. Meem. Full stop.

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:41.270
Is that a sentence?

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:45.670
I don't know if it is, and I don't know if it's not. Only Allah knows what that means.

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:48.260
Okay, check out this one.

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:51.360
The first aayah of Surah al-Rahman is what?

00:20:52.740 --> 00:20:55.380
اَلرَّحْمَان.
It's one word. Is one word a sentence?

00:20:56.640 --> 00:20:57.950
One word is not a sentence.

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:00.350
By the way, in English,

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:02.860
Allah taught the Quran.

00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:04.460
That's a sentence, right?

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:07.050
But if you just say, Allah.

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:09.760
Is that a sentence?

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:11.480
No.

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:13.280
Sometimes there are aayaat

00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:15.100
that are less than a sentence.

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:16.670
They're just a word.

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:19.200
So you can't call an aayah a sentence.

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:22.660
Sometimes there are three aayaat,

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:26.100
and they go together to make one sentence.

00:21:26.110 --> 00:21:27.820
الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ

00:21:27.820 --> 00:21:29.000
الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:30.010
مَالِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:31.690
is one sentence.

00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:33.710
All of that is actually one sentence.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:38.370
Sometimes you have aayaat that have ten

00:21:38.370 --> 00:21:41.980
sentences inside one, or nine sentences inside one aayaah.

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:44.420
ٱللَّهُ لَاۤ إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ٱلۡحَیُّ ٱلۡقَیُّومُ

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:46.340
لَا تَأۡخُذُهُۥ سِنَةࣱ وَلَا نَوۡمࣱ

00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:48.030
لَهُۥ مَا فِی ٱلسَّمَـٰوَ ٰ⁠تِ وَمَا فِی ٱلۡأَرۡضِ

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:52.670
all the way to the end, all of those nine sentences belong inside how many aayahs?

00:21:53.240 --> 00:21:56.110
One aayah. So sometimes an aayah is less than a sentence.

00:21:56.120 --> 00:21:59.590
Sometimes an aayah or multiple aayahs make up one sentence.

00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:02.270
Sometimes lots of aayaat are inside

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:05.850
one sentence. So it is impossible for me to call the aayah a

00:22:06.340 --> 00:22:07.100
sentence.

00:22:08.040 --> 00:22:10.170
I can't call it verse and I can't call it

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:11.350
sentence.

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:14.050
We have to call it something. I have an idea.

00:22:14.640 --> 00:22:15.860
We should call it aayah.

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:20.160
It is unique.

00:22:21.140 --> 00:22:24.380
It is unique. Nothing else has the definition of

00:22:24.550 --> 00:22:24.950
aayah.

00:22:25.440 --> 00:22:28.260
But you still want to translate it in your head, don't you?

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:30.360
What should we, how should we translate

00:22:30.840 --> 00:22:31.270
aayah.

00:22:32.440 --> 00:22:35.060
And so today and in part of this introduction,

00:22:35.070 --> 00:22:37.860
even though I didn't give you a detailed discussion about surah,

00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:38.820
I will do that tomorrow.

00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:42.360
You know why I will do that tomorrow? Any guess? Any guess?

00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:45.670
Why will I talk about surah tomorrow and aayah today?

00:22:47.340 --> 00:22:50.960
Today is micro. Tomorrow is

00:22:51.340 --> 00:22:53.020
macro. And surah is macro.

00:22:53.150 --> 00:22:54.070
So we'll talk about surah

00:22:54.100 --> 00:22:58.270
tomorrow. But at least we have to talk about aayah today. We'll start with that today.

00:22:59.740 --> 00:23:02.950
It is one of the most fascinating words of the Arabic language.

00:23:03.340 --> 00:23:03.960
The word aayah.

00:23:05.040 --> 00:23:07.860
And I will not write this on the screen because

00:23:08.540 --> 00:23:11.000
I'm lazy and also because I want you to take notes.

00:23:12.920 --> 00:23:14.670
The word aayah, the root letters,

00:23:15.040 --> 00:23:16.950
are hamza, yaa, and yaa.

00:23:17.840 --> 00:23:19.360
Hamza, yaa, and yaa.

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:22.670
Amazing word of the Arabic language.

00:23:23.440 --> 00:23:26.860
What other words come from the word that we get aayah from?

00:23:29.440 --> 00:23:32.630
Let me tell you, before I give you the, there are two sides to look at this.

00:23:33.240 --> 00:23:36.930
The one thing is, we're gonna look at the word aayah from the language perspective,

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:38.490
which I'll share with you in a second.

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:40.790
But I want to share something about the word aayah with you

00:23:40.790 --> 00:23:42.130
from the Quran's perspective.

00:23:42.130 --> 00:23:43.930
I want you to appreciate something about the word aayah.

00:23:43.940 --> 00:23:46.270
It's amazing. One of the most amazing things I've

00:23:46.270 --> 00:23:48.060
ever learned about the Quran this whole year,

00:23:48.640 --> 00:23:50.250
this last year, is the word aayah.

00:23:51.140 --> 00:23:52.480
It's one of the most amazing lessons.

00:23:53.840 --> 00:23:55.760
So the Quran says that

00:23:56.140 --> 00:23:56.880
its

00:23:57.040 --> 00:23:57.760
unit,

00:23:58.340 --> 00:24:00.470
its units are aayaat. Yes?

00:24:01.240 --> 00:24:02.950
بَلۡ هُوَ ءَایَـٰتُۢ بَیِّنَـٰتࣱ

00:24:03.340 --> 00:24:03.970
The Quran is just

00:24:03.970 --> 00:24:05.440
ءَایَـٰتُۢ بَیِّنَـٰتࣱ

00:24:06.540 --> 00:24:09.180
Allah says that 'Eesa ('alayhissalaam) is an aayah.

00:24:09.298 --> 00:24:11.063
وَلِنَجۡعَلَكَ ءَایَةࣰ لِّلنَّاسِ

