One of the reasons they traveled outside of the city was

00:58:30.450 --> 00:58:34.950
because they were trying to capture and record the original language,

00:58:35.920 --> 00:58:37.573
the original language. Like al-Asma'ee,

00:58:37.640 --> 00:58:40.330
one of my favorite guys, I'll tell you a story about al-Asma'ee.

00:58:40.920 --> 00:58:42.750
He's kind of, رَحِمَهُ الله,

00:58:43.120 --> 00:58:44.060
I want to go to Jannah,

00:58:44.060 --> 00:58:46.660
one of my motivations is I want to meet al-Asma'ee because

00:58:46.660 --> 00:58:49.150
he is one of the funniest people I've ever read about.

00:58:49.620 --> 00:58:50.840
He is hilarious.

00:58:51.320 --> 00:58:54.250
You know, when people study for a long time, they become a little strange.

00:58:55.920 --> 00:58:58.670
If you spend your life in the library, you become a little weird, like, you know,

00:58:58.670 --> 00:59:00.450
you're socially awkward kind of thing.

00:59:00.820 --> 00:59:03.150
He was, رَحِمَهُ الله, socially awkward.

00:59:04.020 --> 00:59:06.240
He did not care what came in his mouth. He just said it.

00:59:07.620 --> 00:59:11.200
So he used to write a journal of his travels. He's learning Arabic, right?

00:59:11.200 --> 00:59:13.370
So he's traveling. And he wrote his journal.

00:59:13.370 --> 00:59:17.320
He was traveling somewhere and he came across a man. He says,

00:59:17.320 --> 00:59:19.650
I came across a man who was really ugly.

00:59:21.720 --> 00:59:26.150
