00:59:47.720 --> 00:59:50.750
He wrote that down too. A normal 'aalim would not write that down.

00:59:51.220 --> 00:59:53.740
This is al-Asma'ee. He doesn't care.

00:59:54.820 --> 00:59:57.750
And then he wrote down, and when she left the room,

00:59:58.110 --> 01:00:01.580
I talked to, and she could still hear him from the kitchen, he talked to the husband.

01:00:01.590 --> 01:00:02.830
He said, كَيفَ هَذَا

01:00:03.610 --> 01:00:04.640
How did this happen?

01:00:04.640 --> 01:00:07.140
[laughs]

01:00:10.710 --> 01:00:12.680
See, that's al-Asma'ee, he doesn't care.

01:00:12.680 --> 01:00:15.140
Like, I don't understand this situation here.

01:00:15.600 --> 01:00:17.640
Does she have vision problems or...?

01:00:18.010 --> 01:00:20.320
[laughs]

01:00:20.710 --> 01:00:22.030
So she got angry at him.

01:00:22.910 --> 01:00:25.940
She, from the kitchen, got angry at him and she said,

01:00:26.070 --> 01:00:27.940
you should have taqwaa of Allah.

01:00:28.410 --> 01:00:31.810
Maybe he was really good to Allah, and I am his reward.

01:00:31.820 --> 01:00:34.420
Or maybe I was really bad and he's my punishment.

01:00:34.428 --> 01:00:39.800
[laughs]

01:00:40.410 --> 01:00:44.960
So I brought up al-Asma'ee because he actually went on these strange journeys,

01:00:44.970 --> 01:00:45.830
only to do what?

01:00:46.910 --> 01:00:48.440
To capture the old Arabic.

01:00:48.810 --> 01:00:52.250
Because the city was still speaking Arabic. It's true.

01:00:52.260 --> 01:00:57.140
The city was still speaking Arabic, but it wasn't as pure as the Arabic of the

01:00:57.810 --> 01:00:58.470
desert.

01:00:58.660 --> 01:01:01.290
Now, why is it important to protect the Arabic of the desert?

01:01:01.330 --> 01:01:04.530
It was important because the Quran came in the Arabic of the

01:01:05.110 --> 01:01:07.930
desert. I want to leave you with a visual.

